WEBVTT

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:06.020
<i>Everyone is searching for a new world</i>

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:12.120
<i>to attain that overflowing dream.</i>

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:17.700
<i>They all jump over the horizon,</i>

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:26.470
<i>regardless of what lies beyond.</i>

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:34.210
<i>We've run,</i>

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:36.680
<i>we've dived into hope,</i>

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.550
<i>and forgotten only courage.</i>

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:44.290
<i>And we've been swept away by the crowd</i>

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:48.950
<i>only to lose something dear to us.</i>

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.630
<i>I smile with a twisted face,</i>

00:00:54.630 --> 00:01:01.300
<i>and it was the best smile I could put on.</i>

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:04.680
<i>The inside of my mask overflowed with tears</i>

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:12.320
<i>so I covered my wet mask
with yet another mask.</i>

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:17.220
<i>I continue to walk through
the flat battleground,</i>

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:22.460
<i>and I struggle, unable to warp.</i>

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:32.570
<i>The dream waits quietly on a cape far away.</i>

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:37.310
<i>Even if I fumble around clumsily,</i>

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:42.040
<i>I'm sure I'll still be
able to make it there.</i>

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:57.750
I'm leaving for L.A.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.750
We'll be out of contact
for a short while.

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:01.380
Take care of Rio.

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:12.660
Celebrities sure are busy...

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:27.140
"Unwelcome Visitors"

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:50.830
Please stay out of them.
They're police business.

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:54.470
<i>I can't let her get
any further involved</i>

00:02:54.470 --> 00:02:58.670
<i>with the Blade Children or my brother...</i>

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:02.900
<i>But she glares at me from the shadows...</i>

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:08.550
<i>Narumi-san! Narumi-san! Narumi-san!</i>

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:12.350
So here you are!

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:14.420
This is bad! Really bad!

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:17.410
Quiet. Don't spoil my lunch.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:25.230
This is another super-fancy boxed lunch

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:27.430
that would be a waste to eat alone!

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:28.730
<i>Narumi-san!</i>

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:33.040
But this isn't the time
to be goofing around!

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.740
<i>It's terrible, Narumi-san!</i>

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:37.280
There was a new 2nd-year
transfer student today!

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.650
Come to think of it,
you said that this morning...

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:42.150
That transfer student is bad news!

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:44.550
What's the big deal
about a transfer student?

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:50.750
Asazuki?!

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:53.160
Yo.

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:56.160
What are you doing here?!

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:57.730
You can't tell?

00:03:57.730 --> 00:04:00.290
Starting today, I'm a
student at Tsukiomi Academy.

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:09.300
<i>That's right! Asazuki-san is
the one who transferred here!</i>

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:13.010
-Hey.
-Yes?

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:16.750
I thought he disappeared
during middle school.

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:18.650
So where could he have
transferred from?

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:20.420
He's a big fraud!

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:22.690
He even got a really good
score on the transfer exam!

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:25.490
I'll have you know I took
the exam fair and square.

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:26.830
Little Narumi.

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:30.260
This means that starting today
I'm a senior student to you.

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:33.630
<i>You will respectfully refer
to me as Asazuki-senpai.</i>

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:34.840
Yeah, right!

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:36.340
He would never do that!

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:38.840
<i>I'm a senior student to him,</i>

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:43.080
<i>and he's never once
called me Yuizaki-senpai!</i>

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:45.950
He always just says,
"Hey," or, "You!"

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:47.950
That doesn't matter here.

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:51.290
Asazuki...What are you planning?

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:53.920
I somehow doubt you
transferred here as a joke.

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:55.910
Don't tell me...

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:01.700
...there's somebody you
want dead at this school?

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:03.130
Perhaps.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:07.200
I could take care of
a person or two if...

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:12.930
No causing trouble on your
first day here, Kosuke!

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:15.980
Ow!

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:18.910
Ryoko! Are you trying to kill me?!

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:23.120
As if you'd die so easily! Now get up!

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:26.250
Damn...A flying kick out of nowhere...

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:28.260
You're a man; stop your complaining!

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:31.830
Lunch break doesn't last long.
Go buy me some bread!

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:32.860
Bread?

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:37.060
It's what I eat for lunch.
Now get going!

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:39.270
Why should I have to...

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:42.290
Just go get some!

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:50.310
Dammit!

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:54.780
Sorry about that.

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:58.310
I'll put a collar around Kosuke,
so overlook him for a while.

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:01.720
Don't tell me you're...

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:04.360
That's right, I'm one
of the Blade Children.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:06.760
Ryoko Takamachi.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:08.900
I've heard about you two.

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:11.770
I'd suggest you keep low for a while.

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:13.570
What does that mean?

00:06:13.570 --> 00:06:18.830
Have fun while you still can.

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:20.700
See ya!

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:29.420
Hey. What exactly's
about to take place?

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:30.970
You got me...

00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:35.660
Here, I bought you some bread.

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:37.390
Good job!

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:40.260
I've heard the rumors...

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:42.530
<i>Is that Kiyotaka's little brother?</i>

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:45.730
Pretty charming for
the bastard's bro, huh?

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:47.330
I don't know.

00:06:47.330 --> 00:06:49.300
People like that usually
keep something mysterious

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:52.100
living at the bottom of their hearts.

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:00.910
Ryoko.

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:05.250
Sorry for getting you involved.

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:07.960
You probably won't believe me,

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:11.910
but you were the last person
I wanted to get involved.

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:21.960
Kosuke! Have you gotten taller?!

00:07:25.140 --> 00:07:29.140
You have! Just a while ago I was taller!

00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:32.110
You've been watching
your calcium intake, huh?!

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:34.410
That's rude even for you, Kosuke!

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:40.020
I'll surpass you soon enough!

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:47.260
You haven't changed a bit, Ryoko...

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:02.310
Massacre is our destiny.

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:07.470
We Blade Children are
children who must not live.

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:12.750
<i>We must not live?</i>

00:08:14.450 --> 00:08:16.460
<i>If so, Kanone...</i>

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:19.320
<i>...then why were we born?</i>

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:29.800
Assistant Inspector Narumi.

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:32.040
Senior Superintendent Kanzaka!

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:36.680
May I have word with you?

00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:37.940
Yes...

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:49.090
Let's do the next sentence structure.

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:51.990
"Not only you, but he is right."

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:54.530
This structure's going to be on the test.

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:58.800
<i>-The nerve of her...
-"Not only A, but B."</i>

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:01.770
"Thanks for the boxed lunch! Hiyono"
"Not only A, but B."

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:08.740
<i>-She stole yet another lunch from me...
-So the example sentence
would translate as...</i>

00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:13.480
This is an important sentence
structure, so expect it on the test.

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:27.190
Hello!

00:09:27.190 --> 00:09:29.460
<i>Huh? Rio-san?</i>

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:33.160
<i>Hiyono-san?</i>

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:38.670
<i>Rio-san? What were you doing down there?</i>

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:41.940
Oh, were you playing
Hide-and-Seek by yourself?

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:46.210
You can't play "Hide-and-Seek"
with only one person.

00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:47.850
<i>That's strange...</i>

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:51.310
<i>I could swear I sensed bloodlust
coming from behind the door...</i>

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:57.120
<i>What are you doing skipping class,
Hiyono-san?</i>

00:09:57.960 --> 00:09:59.360
Ta-dah!

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:01.760
<i>It's one of Narumi-san's boxed lunches!</i>

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:04.930
They're so wonderful that it's
a waste to eat them all alone,

00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:06.370
so I brought one!

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:08.100
Let's eat it together!

00:10:12.810 --> 00:10:15.100
-Delicious!
-Delicious!

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:29.610
<i>-I want to marry him!
-I want to marry him!</i>

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:42.870
<i>Those aren't the normal doctors!</i>

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:44.340
<i>-Run, Hiyono-san!
-Run, Rio-san!</i>

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:55.370
<i>What the?!</i>

00:10:55.850 --> 00:10:59.090
<i>No! I let my guard down!</i>

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:01.450
<i>These people are Hunters!</i>

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:17.470
<i>Something's beginning...</i>

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:24.570
<i>But what?</i>

00:11:33.550 --> 00:11:35.820
<i>I guess my only choice
is to ask her...</i>

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:39.130
"Rio Takeuchi"

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:41.220
"Rio Takeuchi"
Hey, Rio. We're coming in.

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:44.700
I hear you're still as short as ever?

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:45.670
Huh?

00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:49.440
Rio?

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:52.370
Where in the world did she go?

00:11:52.370 --> 00:11:56.140
Did Rio mention anything to
you about a room change today

00:11:56.140 --> 00:11:57.810
or having a checkup somewhere?

00:11:57.810 --> 00:11:59.680
Both seem unlikely.

00:12:06.350 --> 00:12:10.150
What does that mean, Little Narumi?!

00:12:12.990 --> 00:12:15.100
You can't tell?

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:17.500
Judging from these circumstances,

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:19.970
there's a high probability
she was taken away.

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:26.060
Very shortly, even more
dangerous Hunters will appear...

00:12:28.110 --> 00:12:30.940
<i>So the Hunters that
Rutherford talked about...</i>

00:12:30.940 --> 00:12:32.840
<i>finally showed up...</i>

00:12:37.180 --> 00:12:38.910
Were these your Hunters?

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:43.390
It would seem so.

00:12:43.390 --> 00:12:46.460
This is none of your business. Get lost!

00:12:46.460 --> 00:12:50.400
Take my advice.
You'd best stay out of this.

00:12:50.400 --> 00:12:54.600
Yeah. I'd like to be uninvolved,
if I could.

00:12:55.570 --> 00:12:56.660
But...

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:06.840
The fact that this is here
means that she was here.

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:11.240
<i>If so, then this is my business.</i>

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:25.200
<i>We've been caught, Rio-san...</i>

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:26.800
Thanks to you.

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:28.870
Now that you mention it,
the air in the room

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:32.430
did seem kind of gloomy and tense...

00:13:33.610 --> 00:13:37.340
<i>I can't believe I let my guard down!</i>

00:13:37.340 --> 00:13:40.050
<i>Ahh! Narumi-san's boxed lunch!</i>

00:13:40.050 --> 00:13:42.450
I only got to take a single bite!

00:13:42.450 --> 00:13:45.590
I worked so hard to steal it, too!

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:47.220
<i>By the way, Hiyono-san.</i>

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:49.890
What information did you
come to gather today?

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:51.460
Huh?

00:13:51.460 --> 00:13:55.660
I doubt you only came to
bring the boxed lunch, right?

00:13:55.660 --> 00:13:57.360
Let me think...

00:13:57.360 --> 00:13:59.930
It just seemed to me
that the Blade Children

00:13:59.930 --> 00:14:03.770
were acting strangely frantic lately...

00:14:05.770 --> 00:14:08.580
I have a mountain of
questions I'd like to ask you,

00:14:08.580 --> 00:14:10.980
but I can't take notes in this condition

00:14:10.980 --> 00:14:13.000
so I'll save them for another time!

00:14:14.250 --> 00:14:18.050
Say, where are we, anyway?

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:27.750
My guess would be an abandoned hotel.

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:31.260
It's what we call everyone
who's ever been hostile to us...

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:35.720
In other words, everyone who's
tried to kill the Blade Children.

00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:39.670
People who hunt down
the Blade Children...

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:43.040
Hunters...

00:14:50.380 --> 00:14:54.550
So, in other words, guys like him
are going to start showing up?

00:14:54.550 --> 00:14:56.390
Kosuke! Where's Rutherford?!

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:58.890
He left for L.A. This morning.

00:14:58.890 --> 00:15:02.200
Just our luck, at a time like this...

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:04.260
<i>We'll be out of contact
for a short while.</i>

00:15:04.260 --> 00:15:06.330
<i>Take care of Rio.</i>

00:15:06.330 --> 00:15:07.770
<i>Damn it...</i>

00:15:07.770 --> 00:15:09.760
<i>I won't let Rio be hunted!</i>

00:15:14.070 --> 00:15:15.910
What's this?!

00:15:15.910 --> 00:15:18.080
"They're in the Excellent Hotel.

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:20.480
Rescue them by midnight

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:22.120
or they'll be blown to pieces."

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:24.250
It's from the Hunters!

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:26.650
Seven hours left!

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:28.180
Seven hours?!

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:31.250
Excellent Hotel.

00:15:32.390 --> 00:15:36.330
That's the abandoned hotel
on the outskirts of town...

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:46.070
It's getting dark outside...

00:15:52.610 --> 00:15:55.220
<i>Rio-san? What's wrong?</i>

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:57.250
Are you alright?!

00:15:57.250 --> 00:15:59.890
I'm fine. It doesn't hurt that much...

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:02.120
You don't sound fine to me!

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:05.730
Let's ask the kidnappers to
get you a doctor right away!

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:06.990
That would be pointless.

00:16:06.990 --> 00:16:07.890
No!

00:16:07.890 --> 00:16:12.230
As kidnappers, it's their duty
to treat their hostages with care!

00:16:12.230 --> 00:16:14.960
Plus you're injured!

00:16:16.300 --> 00:16:19.170
<i>They want me dead.</i>

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:41.830
<i>The hunters and the hunted...</i>

00:16:41.830 --> 00:16:44.460
<i>The cursed battle of the cursed people</i>

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:49.370
<i>will forever continue until
one finally dies out.</i>

00:16:49.370 --> 00:16:54.540
<i>Our fight is not nearly as clean...</i>

00:16:54.540 --> 00:17:00.150
<i>"Kill before being killed!"
That's how every day is for us!</i>

00:17:00.150 --> 00:17:03.380
<i>Being scared and running
away is the same as death.</i>

00:17:03.380 --> 00:17:05.320
<i>A terrible fate will simply snatch away</i>

00:17:05.320 --> 00:17:07.950
<i>that which you desire and hold dear</i>

00:17:07.950 --> 00:17:11.160
<i>and slay your spirit and mind!</i>

00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:14.920
<i>It's all over once we
turn our back to fate.</i>

00:17:23.240 --> 00:17:27.070
If they do want you dead,

00:17:27.070 --> 00:17:31.310
then I don't understand why
they have us tied up here.

00:17:31.310 --> 00:17:34.280
They didn't need to bring us here,

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:38.550
they could have disposed
of us back then.

00:17:42.820 --> 00:17:45.020
But they didn't.

00:17:45.020 --> 00:17:48.620
If they do have a reason
to keep me alive, then...

00:17:57.870 --> 00:17:59.970
There's no sneaking in from the back.

00:17:59.970 --> 00:18:02.010
There are mines buried
all over the place.

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:04.310
Mines?!

00:18:04.310 --> 00:18:07.980
All of the 1st-floor doors we
could sneak through are locked

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:10.150
and rigged with wires.

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:12.950
The instant we open one, we go boom.

00:18:12.950 --> 00:18:15.560
The same goes for the windows.

00:18:15.560 --> 00:18:18.690
Looks like the only unrigged
one is the front door.

00:18:18.690 --> 00:18:22.130
In other words, "Come through
the front door fair and square?"

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:28.570
The lights are on!

00:18:28.570 --> 00:18:32.240
Which means the power source works.

00:18:32.240 --> 00:18:34.240
-This is a trap!
-A trap?

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:37.580
The Hunters weren't after just me!

00:18:37.580 --> 00:18:40.710
They plan to round us all
up in one big haul!

00:18:40.710 --> 00:18:45.350
Been expecting us, huh?
Alright, you're on!

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:47.850
It's fine to accept
their challenge and all,

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:51.760
but there's no question they
have traps waiting for us.

00:18:56.860 --> 00:18:58.660
The game begins.

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:18.180
Are they trying to lure us?

00:19:18.180 --> 00:19:21.220
Lure?! Give me a break!

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:23.350
Just answer it, will you?!

00:19:24.520 --> 00:19:26.730
What should we do?!

00:19:26.730 --> 00:19:30.790
You're probably with me because
the Hunters didn't expect you.

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:40.310
The hostages are on the top floor.

00:19:40.310 --> 00:19:41.640
<i>-The top floor?!
-The top floor?!</i>

00:19:44.480 --> 00:19:45.580
Too bad.

00:19:45.580 --> 00:19:48.380
Hey! What do you mean, "Too bad?!"

00:19:53.190 --> 00:19:55.320
I hear something...

00:19:55.320 --> 00:19:58.520
That's what that sound was!
A time bomb!

00:20:04.200 --> 00:20:06.670
Our only choice is to go up! Let's go!

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:09.770
You serious?!

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:11.570
Just run!

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:18.550
Little Narumi probably
won't stand by quietly

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:21.410
once he learns you've
been caught up in this!

00:20:21.410 --> 00:20:24.980
Then I haven't been entirely useless!

00:20:28.890 --> 00:20:31.890
-Will you hear me out?
-I'm all ears.

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:34.560
It's about the old man...

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:36.700
Senior Superintendent Kanzaka?

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:38.800
I work my butt off doing my job,

00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:43.300
and then he tells me,
"You would be better suited elsewhere."

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:45.170
That's terrible!

00:20:45.910 --> 00:20:49.180
Say, what do you usually
do on your days off?

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:50.710
I wash my car.

00:20:50.710 --> 00:20:54.410
-Your car, huh?
-Yes...

00:20:54.410 --> 00:20:58.520
Why do I get counseled to quit
early while you do just fine?!

00:20:58.520 --> 00:21:00.490
Don't look at me!

00:21:01.120 --> 00:21:03.920
I won't need dinner tonight...

00:21:03.920 --> 00:21:05.790
Here you are, one vinegar cucumber!

00:21:05.880 --> 00:21:11.590
<i>A sweet scent washes into my throat</i>

00:21:11.590 --> 00:21:18.290
<i>and my feelings continuously overflow...</i>

00:21:30.410 --> 00:21:36.450
<i>Don't look at me with that same gaze</i>

00:21:36.450 --> 00:21:42.090
<i>that's like you're following a soccer ball.</i>

00:21:42.090 --> 00:21:47.990
<i>I've already grown used to
my third year at the office,</i>

00:21:47.990 --> 00:21:54.570
<i>but did I lose something instead?</i>

00:21:54.570 --> 00:22:00.310
<i>Those days long ago when we
would talk about anything...</i>

00:22:00.310 --> 00:22:05.510
<i>We're finally old enough now</i>

00:22:05.510 --> 00:22:11.350
<i>to have those slightly awkward
discussions about love.</i>

00:22:11.350 --> 00:22:22.960
<i>A single day seems so long,
but a whole year ends so quickly.</i>

00:22:22.960 --> 00:22:28.730
<i>A whole year seems so short,</i>

00:22:28.730 --> 00:22:35.040
<i>but how well will I be able
to live the rest of my life?</i>

00:22:39.030 --> 00:22:41.330
Time for Hiyono's Useful News Report!

00:22:41.330 --> 00:22:43.430
Cloud-wrack to the moon,
wind to flowers!

00:22:43.430 --> 00:22:47.710
Relations and silhouettes
stick with you!

00:22:47.710 --> 00:22:50.140
Next episode's highlight is
a charming and telling song

00:22:50.140 --> 00:22:52.280
performed by the singing sensation,
Hiyo Hiyo!

00:22:52.280 --> 00:22:54.250
If you're a ship, then I'm the port.

00:22:54.250 --> 00:22:58.450
Waiting for you is painful,
but I'll endure it!

00:22:58.450 --> 00:23:00.620
On the next Spiral: Bond of Reasoning...

00:23:00.620 --> 00:23:01.950
Scanner of Darkness

00:23:01.950 --> 00:23:03.990
You can break one arrow,
but you can't break three!

00:23:03.990 --> 00:23:05.960
That's all for today's
Hiyono's Playhouse!
